|> Exercise
    handle=_double_pre_processing_steps_

    Let $A, B \in \rr$, $f : \rr \ra \rr$.
    Rewrite the two compositions below in the form

    $$
    x \ra \dots
    $$

    and describe how the graph of
    each composition relates to the graph of 
    $f$.

    |> Image
        src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing.svg

    |> Solution

        The first composition is
        $$
        x \ra f(B(x + A))
        $$
        per this illustration:

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_stops_1.svg

        The second composition is
        $$
        x \ra f(Bx + A)
        $$
        per this illustration:

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_stops_2.svg

        Insofar as the second part of the question,
        recall that by Exercise 40, gluing this box...

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_Bz_alone.svg

        ...to the right of any function compresses
        the graph of that function horizontally by a
        factor $B$, whereas gluing this box...

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_Au_alone.svg

        ...to the right of any function translates the
        graph of that function by $A$ to the left; so the 
        graph of the first composition...

        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_Bz_mid.svg

        ...where we glue the “$z \ra Bz$” box first and
        the “$u \ra u + A$” box second (starting from $f$
        as the “base box” onto which others are glued—because
        the problem asks how the graph $y = f(x)$ is affected,
        we have to start there), will be...

        __the graph of $f$ horizontally compressed by $B$,
        |> br
        translated left by $A$__
            
        ...while the graph of the second composition...
        
        |> Image
            src=images/svg_ch5_ex_double_pre_processing_Au_mid.svg

        ...where we glue the boxes onto $f$ in the opposite
        order, with the “$z \ra Bz$” box glued second and the 
        “$u \ra u + A$” box glued first, will be...

        __the graph of $f$ translated left by $A$,
        |> br
        horizontally compressed by $B$__

        ...which is slightly different!
